<a name="oracleloginattempts"/><h1>Login Attempts</h1>

<p>After a failed login, the Oracle protocol module lets the client retry on the same connection, as a real Oracle server does.  The <i>maxloginattempts</i> option sets how many attempts a connection gets before it is dropped.  If unset or 0, it defaults to 3, matching Oracle's default.</p>

